  "headline": "Structural-layer schema/runtime parity CORROBORATED (16/16); lexical/resource-layer parity REFUTED - runtime is a strict reject-superset over 6 input classes the schema-over-permissive-parser accepts.",
  "hypothesis": {
    "interpretation": "On the STRUCTURAL layer (candidate object / candidate_id / candidate_type / payload binding / chemistry-v2 gate) the declarative JSON Schema and the Rust runtime are byte-for-byte equivalent deciders over the corpus. On the LEXICAL/RESOURCE layer the equivalence FAILS in a bounded, security-relevant direction: the runtime is a strict REJECT-superset, refusing 6 classes of input (IEEE-754 non-finite numbers, duplicate keys, >8 MiB size, >64 nesting depth, >100000 collection width) that a conformant JSON-Schema validator over a permissive RFC-8259-superset parser ACCEPTS. JSON Schema validates already-parsed values and cannot express these lexical/resource constraints; the runtime front door is therefore NECESSARY and not replaceable by schema validation alone.",
    "lexical_resource_layer": "REFUTED",
    "statement": "runtime and JSON Schema accept and reject the same finite typed corpus",
    "structural_layer": "CORROBORATED",
    "verdict": "PARTIALLY_REFUTED"
  },
